{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>But he shall take a woman in her virginity</b> — the meaning is: but not one who has had intercourse (be'ulah), and this is a negative prohibition that emerges from the implication of a positive command. Afterward He gave a negative prohibition concerning the widow and the disqualified women, and said, \"But a virgin of his own people he shall take as a wife\" (Leviticus 21:14), to command him that he must take one. This is what our Rabbis said (Horayot 11a): he is prohibited by a negative command concerning the widow and commanded by a positive command concerning the virgin. And thus we learned in Torat Kohanim (Sifra, chapter 2:6): \"But a virgin\" — this teaches that he is commanded concerning the virgin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:57:18.769045785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}